name unicode-property-value-aliases
# The standard's own list of what each property's values stand for: the property, the value's short name, its long name.
# The header:
#   "First Field: The first field describes the property for which that property value name is used."
#   "Second Field: The second field is the short name for the property value."
#   "Third Field: The third field is the long name for the property value, typically the formal name used in
#    documentation about the property value."
#   "In the case of Canonical_Combining_Class (ccc), there are 4 fields: The second field is numeric, the third is the
#    short name, and the fourth is the long name."
#   "The above are the preferred aliases. Other aliases may be listed in additional fields."
# A value is a value within its property: the row's thing is the path of the property and the value's short name
# ([gc, Lu]), and each further name the row writes is a name of that value ([[gc, Lu], Uppercase_Letter]), as
# PropertyAliases.txt's rows pair a property's short name with its long one. The short name is never a relation
# (Laplace-Engine#32).
match PropertyValueAliases.txt

tier row by \n
comment hash
remark hash
padded
names property short long alias...
tier field by ;

thing row property short
content property short long alias
# the long name and every other alias: names of the value, in the standard's own vocabulary of value names
value - long alias
attest row long alias
